•ipconfig - Show network configuration
•ipconfig/all - Show detailed IP information
•ifconfig/release - Release IP address
•ipconfig/renew - Renew IP address
•ipconfig/flushdns - Clear DNS cache
•ping[IP] - Check network connectivity to a server.
•tracert[IP] - Trace route to a destination

•nslookup[domain] - Query DNS for domain details
•netstat-an - Show active network connections
•arp-a - Show ARP cache
•hostname - Display computer name
•getmac - Show MAC address of network adapters
•netuse - Connect to a share resource
•netshare - List shared resource
•netstart - Show service
•netstop - Configure network

                   **Linux Commands**
•ls - List directory contents
•cd - Change directory
•cp - Copy file or directories
•mv - Move / rename files
•mkdir - Create new directory
•rmdir - Remove empty directory
•touch - Create an empty file
•chmod - Change file permissions
•chown - Change file owner and group
•cat - View file contents
•ls-la - hidden files
•pwd - Print working directories
•grep - Search text using patterns
•sudo - Execute commands as super user
•man - Display manual pages
•echo - Display a line of text
•ps - Display currently running process
•kill - Terminate a process using its PID
•top - Display real time system statistics and processes
